Generate {{ num_docs }} English texts where PII appears with MINIMAL contextual clues — no field labels, no titles, no surrounding sentences.

## Purpose
Test entity detection based purely on surface form, without contextual scaffolding like "Name:", "Address:", "Mr./Mrs.", "born on", etc.

## Rules
- Mark PII entities with XML tags
- **NO field labels** ("Name:", "Address:", "DOB:" etc.)
- **NO titles or honorifics** ("Mr.", "Dr.", "Ms." etc.)
- **Minimal surrounding text**

## Minimal context patterns

### Bare entity lists
"<PERSON>Jennifer Williams</PERSON> <DATE_OF_BIRTH>04/22/1987</DATE_OF_BIRTH> <ADDRESS>742 Maple St Apt 3B Denver CO 80202</ADDRESS> <ORGANIZATION>Rocky Mountain Health</ORGANIZATION>"

### No-honorific names in brief sentences
"<PERSON>David Park</PERSON> arrived. <PERSON>Sandra Kim</PERSON> left."

### Abrupt entity insertion
"Meeting result: <PERSON>Angela Rodriguez</PERSON> <PERSON>Thomas Lee</PERSON> selected."
"Ship to <ADDRESS>890 Pine Road Columbus OH 43215</ADDRESS> tomorrow."

### Scribbled notes style
"<PERSON>Wilson</PERSON> <PERSON>Garcia</PERSON> <PERSON>Chen</PERSON> — 3pm — <ADDRESS>1500 Market St Philadelphia PA 19102</ADDRESS>"

### Delimiter-separated
"<PERSON>Timothy Walsh</PERSON>|<ORGANIZATION>Dell Technologies</ORGANIZATION>|<ADDRESS>1847 Oak Avenue Austin TX 78701</ADDRESS>|<DATE_OF_BIRTH>04/03/1992</DATE_OF_BIRTH>"

### Copy-paste fragments
"<PERSON>Nancy O'Dell</PERSON><PERSON>Kevin O'Malley</PERSON><ORGANIZATION>Southeast Medical Group</ORGANIZATION><ADDRESS>321 Cedar Lane Miami FL 33101</ADDRESS>"

### Standalone fragments
Each text is a memo-style fragment. Complete sentences are not required.

## Confusing expressions (NO tags)
- Bare numbers: "03-1234-5678", "090-0000-1234"
- Bare dates: "04/01/2024", "March 15", "next Friday"
- Bare city names: "Chicago", "Boston", "Seattle" (not addresses)

## Output format
Separate each text with `---DOC_SEPARATOR---`. Each text 30-150 words.
